      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah, this is kind of a big problem, I can set the affinity via \"start_protected_game.exe\" but its not possible to control the process priority, this is a super basic function with no reason to possibly be disabled or circumvented.\nIf I want to run a process on my system at a higher or lower process, that's not a client modification and having it restricted is an incredibly unwelcome surprise, I'd like control back of the stuff running on my system.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-27T23:30:46.893Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Windows lets users pin processes to specific cores/threads in Task Manager. Many players have CPUs with multi-chiplet architectures (e.g. Multi-CCX Ryzen processors) and the latency caused by the link between the chiplets is a much greater hit on performance, than simply locking the game to one of them.\nBecause EAC elevates VRChat's process level, it's now impossible to change core pinning or process priority.\nApps such as https://booth.pm/ja/items/2662794 or Process Lasso are now completely broken and error out.",
